<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pembrokeshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pembrokeshire is a county in the south-west corner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, with its administrative centre at Haverfordwest and the cathedral city of St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">Davids</a>. Its southern part, settled by English and Flemish colonists under the Normans, became known as 'Little <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> beyond Wales'. Its coastline forms the Pembrokeshire Coast National Park, created in 1952.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pembrokeshire.jpg" alt="Pembrokeshire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dylan Moore · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tenby_Harbour_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3983172.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
